  <section class="content">
    <article>
      <div class="key-points">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Channel is the single strongest predictor of authenticity. Licensed retailer beats marketplace seller every time.</li>
          <li>Every legal import carries an importer label in the local language. No label means no traceable import route.</li>
          <li>The GB/T standard code on the back is the most reliable information on the bottle — it tells you the production method and aroma type.</li>
          <li>Expect to pay 30–100% above Chinese retail once import duty, freight, and distributor margin are included.</li>
          <li>Fakes concentrate in the expensive, famous, giftable end. Buying a $40 bottle is low risk; buying a $200 Moutai is high risk.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

